    1: """NRGPT-style energy recurrence for the Phase 3 architecture seed.
       
       The experiment in REQ-KONA-011 asks a narrow question: if Carnot already has a
       fixed embedding for a FoVer response, does an inference-time energy recurrence
       help a binary verifier more than a plain ContinuousEBM-shaped linear baseline?
       
       This module intentionally stays small and CPU-local.  The energy block is a
       three-linear-layer MLP that is trained to assign higher scalar energy to
       incorrect FoVer responses.  At inference time it refines an embedding by taking
       bounded gradient-descent steps on that learned energy before a linear
       classification head is evaluated.
       
